# Trivy ignore list for infra/terraform.
#
# Every line here is a DELIBERATE, REVIEWED deviation from a security check.
# An uncommented line with no reason is a defect: it makes a finding invisible
# without recording who decided that and why.
#
# policies/scan.sh asserts that the set of ignored IDs is exactly the one below,
# so adding a suppression requires changing that assertion and this file in the
# same review.

# AZU-0013 — Vault network ACL does not block access by default.
#
# DELIBERATE V1 POSTURE, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The V1 profile sets
# public_network_access_enabled = true with network_acls.default_action =
# "Allow" (infra/terraform/modules/keyvault/main.tf). The alternative — a Deny
# default — is worse in V1: there is no private endpoint, and the Container Apps
# workload connects over the public endpoint from addresses that are not covered
# by the AzureServices bypass. A Deny default would therefore lock the workload
# out of its own secrets, turning a security finding into an outage.
#
# REMOVAL CONDITION: this entry MUST be deleted in the same change that sets
# enable_private_network_for_vault = true (the V5 switch). The V5 change also
# inverts invariant KV2 in tests/check_plan_invariants.py, which currently
# asserts the public endpoint IS enabled; the two are coupled and must move
# together.
AZU-0013
